{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Happy</b> — After he likened the sons to arrows to fight against the enemy, he said: \"who fills his quiver with them\" — by way of parable." "<b>They shall not be ashamed</b> — the father and the sons." "<b>And the meaning of \"at the gate\"</b> — before everyone. And the reason to mention this is that David worried when he was told, \"he shall not build the house,\" because his enemies would take vengeance and rejoice. But when Nathan told him that the son who comes forth from his loins shall build the house, all his worry ceased."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 127, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:23.942510450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}